2026-08-09T06:52:05Z   1. SCHEMA: data/uber_daily.csv gains refund_inc_gst (additive, inserted before source; parseCsv and DictReader are header-name based so no reader breaks). Populated from the residual sales-commission-offers-payout; 7 refunds totalling 157.90 across the range. Mirrors adjustments_inc_gst in the weekly feed.
2026-08-09T06:52:05Z   2. BUG FIXED (material, pnl.js): venueDeliveryEst used `uberSplit(...) || uberWeeklyFees(...)`. The daily feed won outright whenever it matched even ONE day in the window, so any window straddling the 2026-07-12/13 feed boundary silently dropped every earlier week. For a 2026-04-05..2026-08-08 Mari window it returned $6,336.51 instead of $39,685.39 - understating delivery cost by $33,348.88, i.e. 84% of the true figure. Delivery cost too LOW flatters the P&L: the failure direction CLAUDE.md warns about. Replaced with uberActual(), which stitches the two feeds on the daily feed's first covered date (daily from there, weekly prorated before it) so neither gap nor overlap is possible.
2026-08-09T06:52:05Z   3. LATENT DOUBLE-COUNT REMOVED (pnl.js): uberSplit added uber_marketing_weekly ads ON TOP of offers_inc_gst. offers_inc_gst IS the portal Marketing line and already contains Uber Ads click spend, so any repopulation of that deprecated (currently empty) file would have double-counted ads. Removed.
2026-08-09T06:52:05Z   4. GUARD ADDED: tests/test_uber_daily.py - 12 assertions, the core one being that each day's arithmetic closes exactly (sales - commission - offers - refund == payout). An estimated commission CANNOT satisfy that identity, so the 33% model cannot creep back without CI going red. Also covers column set, 2dp money, non-negative fees, the 5-33% rate band, zero-sales days being explained rather than zeroed, sort order/uniqueness, and daily-vs-weekly non-overlap.
2026-08-09T06:52:05Z   5. ESCALATION FIXED (scripts/health_monitor.py): new "Uber fee feed" check. This is the actual root cause of the four-week error - the drift WAS detected on 11 consecutive runs and written to THIS log, which nobody reads. It now surfaces on the dashboard health banner: 'down' if the split stops balancing, 'warn' if commission exceeds Uber's 33% ceiling or the feed falls 3+ days behind, each with plain-English meaning/action/selfheal for the management team. Currently reads: ok - exact split, balances on all 48 days.
