2026-08-14T08:06:26Z     (4) THE BACKFILL RAN AND SILENTLY THREW ITSELF AWAY. The ingest self-heal correctly re-dispatched 08-11, 08-12 and Mari 08-13 at 07:51Z and eight Daily Pull runs all reported SUCCESS - none of them landed. Their commit step is: for i in 1 2 3; do git pull --rebase origin main && git push && break || sleep; done. A rebase that fails part-way leaves .git/rebase-merge behind, so attempts 2 and 3 die instantly on "already a rebase-merge directory" and the loop only sleeps; and because it ends in || sleep the step exits 0 regardless. Aggregated, committed, never pushed, reported green. Now aborts a half-rebase before retrying and FAILS the step if work was committed but not pushed. The venue+date concurrency fix (2a30af0) was already in place and was not the problem this time - this was underneath it.
